1
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:07,830
A trailing stop follows the price as it moves in your favour.

2
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:11,950
Right click your trade and choose Trailing Stop.

3
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:15,810
Set Trailing Stop Distance is already ticked.

4
00:00:15,910 --> 00:00:21,880
With trailing on, the stop is set by the distance below, not by this rate.

5
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:25,910
Then choose how far behind the price the stop should follow.

6
00:00:26,010 --> 00:00:32,720
Click OK.

7
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:37,580
The trade now shows its stop, and the trailing distance under TR.STOP.

8
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:42,080
As the price rises, the stop moves up with it. It never moves back down.

